---

<LandingLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  h1={h1}
  lede={lede}
  eyebrow="Walthamstow · Adults"
  pageJsonLd={pageJsonLd}
>
  <h2>What integrative psychotherapy means here</h2>
  <p>
    Integrative psychotherapy means I don’t stick to one rigid template. We draw on
    different modalities — relational talking therapy, Acceptance and Commitment Therapy
    (ACT), and experiential or creative approaches — to find what actually resonates with
    you and your history, adjusting as we go.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you’ve tried therapy before and left feeling stuck, unseen, or sure it “wasn’t for
    you,” it often isn’t that therapy failed. It’s that the approach didn’t match you.
    This practice is built for that second (or third) chance — without starting from
    scratch in the same old way.
  </p>

  <h2>Relational depth, without the jargon trap</h2>
  <p>
    When we work together, you can expect candour and collaboration. Your lived experience
    is held in higher regard than textbook models. I’m interested in functional truth: the
    beliefs we treat as true and act on — even when they cause pain — and how those beliefs
    shape day-to-day behaviour.
  </p>
  <p>
    The goal isn’t to erase hard feelings. It’s to help you drop the struggle with what’s
    keeping you stuck, stay grounded in what matters, and take steps toward a life aligned
    with your values.
  </p>

  <h2>ACT-informed and creatively open</h2>
  <p>
    Much of the work is ACT-informed: building psychological flexibility, untangling from
    unhelpful self-stories, and supporting committed action. Where it helps, we can also
    bring in creative or musical processes — always with clear consent and an agreed frame
    for the session.
  </p>
  <p>
    I am registered with the HCPC as an Arts Therapist / Music Therapist and practise under
    the standards of the National Council of Integrative Psychotherapists (NCIP).
  </p>

  <h2>Practicalities in Walthamstow</h2>
  <p>
    I work across Walthamstow and East London, but I don’t currently hold a fixed clinic
    room. When we begin, we arrange a suitable private space together — somewhere calm
    and practical for the work. Home visits are available where that feels more
    accessible, and online sessions remain an option if that’s the better fit.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Serving Walthamstow, Waltham Forest (E17), and the wider East London area.</li>
    <li>Transparent sliding-scale fees — explore the
      {' '}<a href="/#rates">rates guide</a>
      {' '}on the homepage; the final fee is agreed between us.</li>
    <li>Clear policies for privacy, payment, and therapeutic agreements in the footer.</li>
    <li>A free 15-minute consultation to check fit before committing.</li>
  </ul>
</LandingLayout>
